Installer-BS
============

A parody-but-functional fork of "Installer-SH" by Андрей Цымбалов (Chimbal):
https://github.com/Shedou/Installer-SH

Installer-BS keeps the sensible core idea of the original — root-less portable
software, config isolation, menu integration — and reimplements it cleanly as
modular, dependency-free Bash. Its user-facing texts satirise the archaisms and
the marketing of the original; the code does not.

The original scripts are preserved for reference in docs/legacy/. A guided tour
of what changed and why lives in docs/MUSEUM.md, with the full technical catalog
in docs/dev/ANTIPATTERNS.md.

The original work is MIT-licensed and that copyright is retained in LICENSE.
The satire targets engineering decisions and public claims, not the person.

"BS" expands to BullShit (the honest one), Bash Script (the technical one), or
Bundled Software (the one for release notes). All three are correct.
